
Clam is a Perl AI coding harness modeled on Pi,
with a SQLite backend, and a pub/sub bus
modeled on Marvin Minsky's "Society of Mind".

I want to try a hybrid cognitive architecture...
LLMs for pattern recognition and intuition,
and logic engines for deliberate reasoning,
with a Minsky-style blackboard for coordination.

Why use expensive (and slow) LLMs for those tasks
that could be automated to perl scripts and Logic systems.

It has the beginnings of a plugin system, called Wits.

It's very new and I dunno if it's a good idea,
but it's an AI harness in PERL!



